#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Summit App Store: find, install and look after apps.

Where apps come from:
  Flathub          thousands of apps; they install for you only (no password) with Flatpak, each in its own
                   sandbox, and show up in Launchpad, Spotlight and the dock right away
  Ubuntu           the system's own software library (apt); search finds these too. Asks for your password.
  A file           a .deb, .flatpak/.flatpakref or .AppImage you downloaded: double-click it, or use
                   Options → Install from a File

The store only runs while its window is open (automatic app updates are a small separate timer).

  summit-appstore [--show APP_ID] [--updates] [FILE]
"""
